      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.9,
          "end": 8.71,
          "en": "Now what you'll learn thus far about stores and subscriptions is all true and all knowledge you absolutely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 8.71,
          "end": 11.92,
          "en": "should keep around and knowledge you will use a lot in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.01,
          "end": 16.54,
          "en": "However, if you have a case like this, which is a quite common case, that you simply subscribe and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 16.54,
          "end": 21.4,
          "en": "then you store the data in a variable which you then use in your markup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 21.55,
          "end": 29.26,
          "en": "In such a case, Svelte offers you a shortcut that actually allows you to save all that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 29.26,
          "end": 30.37,
          "en": "Yes, that is correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 30.37,
          "end": 32.62,
          "en": "So you don't need to manage your own subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 32.62,
          "end": 34.18,
          "en": "You don't need to unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 34.18,
          "end": 39.7,
          "en": "Instead, you can use a convenient shortcut which svelte offers you if you have your store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 39.7,
          "end": 45.46,
          "en": "And that store exposes data which you directly want to use in your markup, in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 45.46,
          "end": 51.76,
          "en": "So to say then you don't need to manually set up a subscription and extract the data and store it instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 51.76,
          "end": 59.74,
          "en": "in your markup here where I previously used items, you now just use your store name card items and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 59.74,
          "end": 63.44,
          "en": "you prepend it with a dollar sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 63.71,
          "end": 70.25,
          "en": "Now of course we have no variable that is named dollar sign card items in this component, but for variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 70.25,
          "end": 77.6,
          "en": "starting with a dollar sign, svelte assumes that they are stores and then looks for an object a store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 77.6,
          "end": 78.86,
          "en": "named card items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 78.98,
          "end": 79.64,
          "en": "That's the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 79.64,
          "end": 81.71000000000001,
          "en": "We have a store named card items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 81.71000000000001,
          "end": 87.35,
          "en": "And then what svelte does is behind the scenes, it automatically sets up a subscription, extracts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 87.35,
          "end": 89.53999999999999,
          "en": "the data, then uses the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 89.53999999999999,
          "end": 90.95,
          "en": "Here, I'm using it in a loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 90.95,
          "end": 92.24000000000001,
          "en": "You don't have to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 92.24000000000001,
          "end": 93.89,
          "en": "If it was just a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 93.89,
          "end": 100.13,
          "en": "For example, let's say your store stores, just a string, then you could also just do that and use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
